channel.description:
Course script for School-related IT Infrastructure (teacher training in computer science and digital basic education).
Author: Gerald Landl · Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0
Documentation techniques
Reference chapter: each technique is introduced in the session shown and is then used in all later sessions and in the portfolio. The chapters’ documentation tasks refer to this chapter. Markdown, Git and pull request workflow Network diagrams and IP plans VLAN and permission matrices Runbooks Change logs for device policies Processing register (GDPR) and ADRs {class=“pages pages-tree”}
Virtualization & Containerization
Session: 05.10.2026 · Documentation technique: Markdown, Git and pull request workflow · Homework due: 18.10.2026 This chapter is still a skeleton. Learning goals Theory Guided lab Exercise (school scenario) Documentation task Self-check Homework (graded) Security and data protection Sources {class=“pages pages-tree”}
Networking I
Session: 19.10.2026 · Documentation technique: Network diagrams and IP plans · Homework due: 08.11.2026 This chapter is still a skeleton. Learning goals Theory Guided lab Exercise (school scenario) Documentation task Self-check Homework (graded) Security and data protection Sources {class=“pages pages-tree”}
Networking II
Session: 09.11.2026 · Documentation technique: VLAN and permission matrices · Homework due: 22.11.2026 This chapter is still a skeleton. Learning goals Theory Guided lab Exercise (school scenario) Documentation task Self-check Homework (graded) Security and data protection Sources {class=“pages pages-tree”}
Server Administration
Session: 23.11.2026 · Documentation technique: Runbooks · Homework due: 06.12.2026 This chapter is still a skeleton. Learning goals Theory Guided lab Exercise (school scenario) Documentation task Self-check Homework (graded) Security and data protection Sources {class=“pages pages-tree”}
Client & Mobile Device Management
Session: 07.12.2026 · Documentation technique: Change logs for device policies · Homework due: 13.12.2026 This chapter is still a skeleton. Learning goals Theory Guided lab Exercise (school scenario) Documentation task Self-check Homework (graded) Security and data protection Sources {class=“pages pages-tree”}
IT Security & Data Protection
Session: 14.12.2026 · Documentation technique: Processing register (GDPR) and ADRs This chapter is still a skeleton. Learning goals Theory Capstone case study Exercise (school scenario) Documentation task Self-check Security and data protection Sources {class=“pages pages-tree”}
About this book
Author: Gerald Landl Licence: CC BY-SA 4.0 The English version is machine-translated and reviewed by the author. German is the authoritative version. The content on data protection and youth protection is not legal advice.
Assessment rubric
Portfolio submissions (documentation tasks and homework) are assessed on four criteria: Criterion Description Technical correctness The implementation works and matches the task. Completeness All required parts are present. Documentation quality Clear, well structured, appropriate documentation technique. School-context reflection Data protection and security aspects are considered. Weighting and scoring scheme to follow.
Glossary DE↔EN
Deutsch English Virtualisierung virtualization Container container Berechtigungskonzept permission concept {class=“pages pages-tree”}

